Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is complete when:

World map only loads world-level markers.
City maps load only city-specific markers.
Submaps load only their own data.
Lore follows the same hierarchy as the maps.
Leaflet calibration works for every map type.
Rendering bugs are fixed.
Scale is expressed in miles instead of abstract zoom levels.
Layer visibility changes automatically based on map scale.
There is only one legend.
The chat panel acts as a contextual HUD container.
Notification and chat panels visually merge into one HUD.
The map frame has a thicker, more immersive fantasy atlas appearance.
All behavior is documented under docs/ to serve as the single source of truth.

WorldPanel.tsx Refactor & Dynamic Lore System
Goal

WorldPanel.tsx should become the universal information panel for the entire Atlas system.

Instead of being designed around a single location type, it must dynamically render information for every atlas object regardless of its schema.

The panel should automatically adapt to the selected object without requiring a unique component for every location type.

Supported Atlas Objects

The World Panel must support displaying information for all atlas objects, including but not limited to:

World
Continents
Nations
Regions
Sub Regions
Cities
Districts
Settlements
Villages
Hamlets
Roads
Rivers
Forests
Mountains
Swamps
Wetlands
Deserts
Islands
Oceans
Seas
Lakes
Dungeons
Ruins
Landmarks
Points of Interest
Shrines
Temples
Shops
Taverns
Guilds
Castles
Keeps
Sewers
Interior Maps

The panel should not assume any fixed data structure.

Schema Driven Rendering

Every atlas object already has its own schema.

Examples:

public/assets/atlas/schemas/

forest.schema.json
city.schema.json
region.schema.json
road.schema.json
settlement.schema.json
shop.schema.json
...

Every schema contains different fields.

For example:

A forest contains

biome
dominant trees
wildlife
dangers

A road contains

start
destination
distance
patrol status

A city contains

districts
ruler
government
population
economy
factions

A shop contains

owner
inventory
opening hours
services
prices

The panel must inspect the loaded object and render only the fields that exist.

No hardcoded city layout.

No hardcoded forest layout.

No large switch statements.

Dynamic Sections

Instead of fixed components, the panel should generate sections automatically.

Example

Overview

Description

History

Government

Population

Economy

Travel

Climate

Wildlife

Factions

Religion

Services

Inventory

Quests

Related Locations

Notes

Only sections containing data should be rendered.

Empty sections should never appear.

Shop Support

The World Panel should fully support shops.

When selecting a shop, the panel should display information such as:

owner
shop type
inventory
available services
prices
opening hours
reputation
associated faction
dialogue hooks

The panel should become the foundation for future shop interactions.

Future Extensibility

The renderer should be schema-driven.

Adding a new atlas object should require only:

creating a schema
creating the JSON data

The World Panel should automatically support the new object without requiring additional UI code.

Icon System

Do not use:

react-icons
lucide-react
Hero Icons
Font Awesome

The project already has a centralized icon system.

All icons must be imported from:

src/assets/icons/index.ts

This keeps the visual style consistent throughout the application.

